### 4. API Testing
Test backend endpoints for correctness and security.

#### Tools
- **Vitest**: For API unit tests
- **Supertest**: HTTP assertion library
- **Postman/Insomnia**: Manual API testing

#### Key API Tests
```typescript
import request from 'supertest';
import { app } from '../server/index';

describe('Payment API', () => {
  it('should process UPI payment', async () => {
    const response = await request(app)
      .post('/api/upi/pay')
      .send({
        upiId: 'user@paytm',
        amount: 1000,
        description: 'Flight booking'
      })
      .set('Authorization', 'Bearer <token>');

    expect(response.status).toBe(200);
    expect(response.body.success).toBe(true);
    expect(response.body.transactionId).toBeDefined();
  });

  it('should enforce rate limiting', async () => {
    // Send 21 requests (limit is 20/15min)
    for (let i = 0; i < 21; i++) {
      const response = await request(app)
        .post('/api/upi/pay')
        .send({ upiId: 'user@paytm', amount: 100 });

      if (i === 20) {
        expect(response.status).toBe(429);
        expect(response.body.message).toContain('Too many requests');
      }
    }
  });
});
```

### 5. Load Testing
Simulate high traffic to ensure scalability.

#### Tools
- **K6** (Recommended): Modern load testing
- **Apache JMeter**: Comprehensive testing suite
- **Artillery**: Simple, powerful load testing

#### Load Test Script (K6)
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';

export let options = {
  stages: [
    { duration: '2m', target: 100 },   // Ramp up to 100 users
    { duration: '5m', target: 1000 },  // Ramp up to 1000 users
    { duration: '5m', target: 1000 },  // Stay at 1000 users
    { duration: '2m', target: 0 },     // Ramp down to 0 users
  ],
  thresholds: {
    http_req_duration: ['p(95)<200'],  // 95% of requests under 200ms
    http_req_failed: ['rate<0.01'],    // Error rate under 1%
  },
};

export default function () {
  // Test home page
  let res = http.get('https://your-app.replit.app/');
  check(res, { 'status is 200': (r) => r.status === 200 });

  // Test API
  res = http.post('https://your-app.replit.app/api/upi/pay', {
    upiId: 'test@paytm',
    amount: 1000,
  });
  check(res, { 'payment successful': (r) => r.json('success') === true });

  sleep(1);
}
```

#### Expected Performance Targets
- **Response Time**: p95 < 200ms
- **Throughput**: > 1000 req/sec
- **Error Rate**: < 0.1%
- **Concurrent Users**: 10,000+

### 6. Security Testing
Identify vulnerabilities and ensure data protection.

#### Tools
- **OWASP ZAP**: Automated security scanner
- **Burp Suite**: Manual penetration testing
- **npm audit**: Check dependencies for vulnerabilities

#### Security Test Checklist
```bash
# 1. Dependency Vulnerabilities
npm audit
npm audit fix

# 2. OWASP ZAP Scan
zap-cli quick-scan https://your-app.replit.app

# 3. Manual Tests
- SQL Injection attempts
- XSS payload injection
- CSRF token validation
- Authentication bypass attempts
- Rate limiting verification
- Header security checks
```

#### Security Test Cases
```typescript
describe('Security Tests', () => {
  it('should prevent SQL injection', async () => {
    const response = await request(app)
      .get('/api/bookings')
      .query({ id: "1' OR '1'='1" });

    expect(response.status).not.toBe(200);
  });

  it('should sanitize XSS payloads', async () => {
    const xssPayload = '<script>alert("XSS")</script>';
    const response = await request(app)
      .post('/api/booking/create')
      .send({ name: xssPayload });

    expect(response.body.name).not.toContain('<script>');
  });

  it('should require authentication for protected routes', async () => {
    const response = await request(app).get('/api/my-bookings');
    expect(response.status).toBe(401);
  });
});
```

### 7. Accessibility Testing
Ensure the app is usable by everyone.

#### Tools
- **axe DevTools**: Browser extension
- **WAVE**: Web accessibility evaluation
- **Lighthouse**: Chrome DevTools audit
- **Screen Readers**: NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver

#### Accessibility Checklist
- [ ] All images have alt text
- [ ] Proper heading hierarchy (h1 → h6)
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works
- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG AA (4.5:1)
- [ ] Form labels properly associated
- [ ] ARIA attributes where needed
- [ ] Focus indicators visible
- [ ] No keyboard traps

